<h3>Key Takeaways for Practitioners</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Architecture first:</strong> EAGLE-2's feature prediction loss was a hard data ceiling. Only EAGLE-3 TTT (or DFlash) enables meaningful data scaling. [arXiv:2503.01840]</li>
  <li><strong>1M+ balanced conversations:</strong> The 320K community baseline leaves 23% acceptance length uncaptured. Empirically validated threshold is &asymp;1.4M balanced conversations. [arXiv:2603.18567]</li>
  <li><strong>Regenerate responses with the target model:</strong> T=0.8 for diversity. Both SpecBundle and DFlash independently adopt this. [SpecForge &sect;6; DFlash &sect;4.2]</li>
  <li><strong>Domain coverage predicts per-task acceptance rate:</strong> Math/code coverage in training data maps directly to math/code acceptance rate. SpecBundle achieves 1.61&times;&ndash;4.48&times; better throughput on coding/math specifically. [SpecForge &sect;6.1]</li>
  <li><strong>For diffusion drafters, anchor sampling multiplies data:</strong> DFlash extracts multiple training examples per response via random anchor placement. [DFlash &sect;4.2]</li>
  <li><strong>Long-context alignment matters for reasoning models:</strong> P-EAGLE found reasoning traces hit P90 = 10,800 tokens; drafts trained on short sequences see &asymp;25% acceptance rate drops. [P-EAGLE, arXiv]</li>
</ul>
</section>

<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: The Dataset Recipe for Speculative Decoding Drafters</h2>
    <p>Speculative decoding accelerates LLM inference by having a cheap draft model propose tokens that the main model verifies in parallel. The key metric is acceptance length — how many draft tokens survive verification. Community draft models trained on ShareGPT and UltraChat, roughly 320 thousand conversations of mostly chat content, achieve an acceptance length of 2.82 on math benchmarks. Switching to Open-PerfectBlend — 1.4 million balanced conversations covering chat, math, coding, and instruction following — improves acceptance length to 3.48, a 23 percent gain and 1.17 times inference speedup with no architectural changes.</p>
    <p>But data scaling only works once the architecture allows it. EAGLE-1 and EAGLE-2 predict hidden features rather than tokens directly, creating a data ceiling. EAGLE-3 fixes this by removing the feature prediction loss and adding Training-Time Test. Both SpecForge's SpecBundle and DFlash independently found that regenerating dataset responses using the target model at temperature 0.8 is essential. DFlash additionally uses anchor sampling and exponential positional loss weighting. End-to-end, better data recipes push speedups from about 1.76 times to 4.48 to 4.86 times over baseline autoregressive decoding.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：投机解码草稿模型的数据配方</h2>
    <p>投机解码通过让轻量草稿模型预测多个候选词元、再由主模型并行验证来加速推理，核心指标是接受长度——即每次验证通过的草稿词元数量。社区常用的草稿模型基于ShareGPT加UltraChat共32万条对话训练，在数学任务上的接受长度仅为2.82。换用Open-PerfectBlend——140万条均衡数据——接受长度提升至3.48，相当于23%的增益与1.17倍的推理加速，架构不变。</p>
    <p>然而，数据扩展的前提是架构本身允许受益于更多数据。EAGLE-1/2存在"数据天花板"。EAGLE-3通过移除特征预测损失并引入训练时测试解决了这一问题。SpecForge的SpecBundle与DFlash都独立发现，用目标模型以温度0.8重新生成数据集的回答至关重要。DFlash还额外采用锚点采样和指数位置损失加权。最终，更好的数据配方将端到端速度从约1.76倍提升至4.48到4.86倍。</p>
  </div>
</div>

</article>

